1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:01,378
Meet Demeter.

2
00:00:01,598 --> 00:00:06,695
A spatial design studio that turns orchard planning into a landscape you can
explore.

3
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:13,801
On a hillside, water, sunlight, structures and operating costs are
connected.

4
00:00:14,017 --> 00:00:19,400
Demeter brings those decisions into one computed, three dimensional orchard.

5
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:22,051
Start with a request.

6
00:00:22,271 --> 00:00:24,965
A one hundred sixty by ninety metre orchard.

7
00:00:25,185 --> 00:00:27,228
Twelve metres of elevation change.

8
00:00:27,448 --> 00:00:32,011
Two greenhouses, winter sunlight, and a four metre drone swath.

9
00:00:32,231 --> 00:00:34,657
Structured instructions update the design.

10
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:39,746
The same scene data drives geometry and engineering.

11
00:00:39,966 --> 00:00:42,834
Terrain is reconstructed along terrace boundaries.

12
00:00:43,054 --> 00:00:45,898
One hundred eighty eight trees grow into place.

13
00:00:46,118 --> 00:00:49,079
Foundations, columns and roof panels assemble.

14
00:00:49,299 --> 00:00:53,374
Finally, the water network extends from the source through the orchard.

15
00:00:53,594 --> 00:00:55,196
Each structure has a place.

16
00:00:55,416 --> 00:00:57,483
Every parameter has a consequence.

17
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:05,410
Greenhouse placement follows the available terraces.

18
00:01:05,630 --> 00:01:10,935
The design checks the building footprint, ground variation and separation
from obstacles.

19
00:01:11,155 --> 00:01:17,204
Two protective structures become part of the orchard, with their own light
transmission and construction costs.

20
00:01:18,600 --> 00:01:20,133
Move through the solar day.

21
00:01:20,353 --> 00:01:27,841
Terrain ray tests estimate direct sunlight at each tree, while roof
transmission changes the protected growing conditions.

22
00:01:28,061 --> 00:01:30,789
Compare locations before committing to a layout.

23
00:01:33,600 --> 00:01:40,380
The hydraulic engine evaluates one hundred eight configurations of routes,
pipe sizes, pumps and watering zones.

24
00:01:40,600 --> 00:01:43,816
Fifty eight satisfy this scenario's constraints.

25
00:01:44,036 --> 00:01:50,178
Compare cost, pressure and operating time, then inspect a balanced design in
three dimensions.

26
00:01:51,600 --> 00:01:54,061
Drone sweeps stay within the working area.

27
00:01:54,281 --> 00:01:59,483
Transfer paths route around structures, with spraying switched off between
working segments.

28
00:01:59,703 --> 00:02:03,929
This plan achieves ninety seven point three percent geometric coverage.

29
00:02:06,600 --> 00:02:10,408
Bring investment and annual operations into the same decision.

30
00:02:10,628 --> 00:02:18,825
Adjust price and yield, compare cash flow and five year net present value,
and export the design with its inputs and calculation results.

31
00:02:21,600 --> 00:02:23,552
The planner proposes structured edits.

32
00:02:23,756 --> 00:02:26,408
Validation preserves engineering constraints.

33
00:02:26,613 --> 00:02:28,370
The solver supplies the results.

34
00:02:28,575 --> 00:02:35,400
The model adapter uses this same contract, so the visual experience and the
calculation pipeline stay connected.

35
00:02:36,600 --> 00:02:37,134
Demeter.

36
00:02:37,354 --> 00:02:40,199
From a hillside to an orchard you can understand.

37
00:02:40,419 --> 00:02:44,633
Explore the source, run the project, and build your next design.
